#: src/running-testing.md:3
msgid "Running & Testing"
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:5
msgid ""
"Use this section to run and test code in Zed, then debug issues without "
"leaving the editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:8
msgid "What's here"
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:10
msgid ""
"**[Terminal](./terminal.md)**: Zed's built-in terminal emulator. Open "
"multiple terminals, customize your shell, and integrate with the editor. "
"Tasks and commands run here."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:12
msgid ""
"**[Tasks](./tasks.md)**: Define and run shell commands with access to editor "
"context like the current file, selection, or symbol. Use tasks to build, "
"lint, run scripts, or execute any repeatable workflow."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:14
msgid ""
"**[Debugger](./debugger.md)**: Set breakpoints, step through code, and "
"inspect variables using Zed's built-in debugger. Works with C, C++, Go, "
"JavaScript, Python, Rust, TypeScript, and more through the Debug Adapter "
"Protocol."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:16
msgid ""
"**[REPL](./repl.md)**: Run code interactively using Jupyter kernels. Execute "
"selections or cells and see results inline—useful for Python, TypeScript "
"(Deno), R, Julia, and other supported languages."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:18
msgid "Quick start"
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:20
msgid ""
"**Open a terminal**: Press `` Ctrl+` `` to toggle the terminal panel, or "
"`Ctrl+~` to open a new terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:22
msgid ""
"**Run a command**: Press `Cmd+Shift+R` (macOS) or `Ctrl+Shift+R` (Linux/"
"Windows) to open the task picker, then type any shell command."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:24
msgid ""
"**Start debugging**: Press `Cmd+Shift+D` (macOS) or `Ctrl+Shift+D` (Linux/"
"Windows) to open the debug panel and select a configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/running-testing.md:26
msgid ""
"**Run code interactively**: In a Python or TypeScript file, select some code "
"and press `Ctrl+Shift+Enter` to execute it in a REPL session."
msgstr ""
